      "amount": "1/2 teaspoon"
    },
    {
      "name": "black pepper",
      "amount": "1/4 teaspoon"
    },
    {
      "name": "chopped pistachios",
      "amount": "1/4 cup",
      "notes": "for garnish"
    }
  ],
  "instructions": [
    "Preheat the oven to 400 degrees Fahrenheit.",
    "In a large copper mug, heat the olive oil over medium heat on the stovetop.",
    "Add the chopped onion and cook until translucent, about 5 minutes.",
    "Add the minced garlic and cook for an additional minute, stirring constantly.",
    "Add the katsuobushi, sumac, paprika, salt, and black pepper, and stir to combine.",
    "Add the basmati rice and stir to combine with the katsuobushi mixture.",
    "Transfer the copper mug to the preheated oven and bake for 20 minutes.",
    "Remove the mug from the oven and fluff the pilaf with a fork.",
    "Garnish with chopped pistachios and serve hot."
  ],
